From 048588e93e8093150d20293f307749c05ef7aef0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:38:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] dos: Count HSDir requests from unknown previous hops

Tor builds the circuit of every anonymized directory request, including
each onion service descriptor fetch and upload, through relays in the
consensus, and so does Arti. Nothing counts how often an HSDir sees
otherwise.

Count the onion service directory requests that tor accepts (over an
anonymous circuit, and the first HSDir request on it) whose previous
hop is neither in our consensus nor described by a descriptor we have,
as RefuseUnknownExits checks for exit streams, and export them as
tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_unknown_prev_hop"}. They are a share of
the requests in tor_relay_hsdir_fetch_total and
tor_relay_hsdir_upload_total that are neither single_hop nor refused.
Nothing is refused. The cost is one known-relay lookup per such
request.

Part of #41339.
